      "role": "user",
      "content": "Yeah, I definitely want to avoid anything that looks like redlining, but we need to be able to quantify these things to make the model work. When you mention \"neighborhood stability\" or \"volatility,\" what actual variables are you thinking of? Like, if we're looking at things like residential turnover rates or the types of commercial businesses in a zip code, do those tend to correlate strongly with lower default rates?",
